HENK: this site is linked, but its dev server isn't answering.

Routing and the certificate are fine — henk reached the address you linked
and got nothing usable back. It's almost always one of these three.

  1. The dev server isn't running.
     Start it: npm run dev / sail up / docker compose up -d

  2. It's bound to localhost only.
     Traefik runs in Docker and reaches your machine over IPv4 via
     host.docker.internal, so a server on 127.0.0.1 or [::1] is invisible
     to it. Restart on 0.0.0.0:
     nuxt dev --host / vite --host / next dev -H 0.0.0.0

  3. It rejects the .{{TLD}} hostname.
     Vite-based apps refuse unknown hosts with a 403. Add this host to
     server.allowedHosts in your Vite config.

Don't guess — `henk doctor` probes the port and tells you which one it is.
